<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Brodland (2002) / Krieg et al. (2008) / Maître et al. (2012) Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) and zebrafish germ-layer cortical tension sorting — MorphoEval overall 91.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py` (91.3/100, up from 57.3/100 in Pass 1; +34.0 points). The remediated script implements Brodland's (2002) Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (`compute_dith_tensions`, L97-145), Krieg et al.'s (2008) 4 zebrafish germ-layer perturbation regimes (`wildtype_germ_layer_engulfment` Δr = +0.3807, `camlc_ectoderm_cortex_reversal` Δr = -0.3282, `blebbistatin_myosin_inhibition` |Δr| = 0.0000, and `high_hit_partial_doublet_lens` Δr = +0.1370) plus simultaneous 3-germ-layer concentric stratification (`r_E = 0.870 > r_M = 0.663 > r_N = 0.446`), executes a 7-point continuous sweep across ectodermal cortical tension `beta_E in {25, 50, 72, 95, 115, 130, 145} pN/um` crossing the inversion threshold `beta_E = beta_M = 95 pN/um`, implements Maître et al.'s (2012) Young-Dupré cell-doublet contact angle and normalized contact radius law (`compute_young_dupre_doublet`, L148-190), segments the SHA-256-locked zebrafish blastoderm GFP/RFP cross-transplantation and mushroom doublet specimen (`germ_layer_doublet_specimen.jpg`, radial profile `r = 0.9301, RMSE = 0.1844`, doublet `r_c/R = 0.9717`), and is backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_044_differential_interfacial_tension_sorting.lean`. Overall 91.3/100 (faithfulness 90.9, reproducibility 92.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit b9976f8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 89, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/differential_interfacial_tension_sorting_comparison.png: rendered output of 2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py at b9976f8, image/png, 419495 B, 3000×1260 px, artifact_sha256 68bcaffb42002b53f8666b482f0c8eb740fd840065dd289e2b5fd57b6ee1fefd (sha256 68bcaffb42002b53f8666b482f0c8eb740fd840065dd289e2b5fd57b6ee1fefd), spec_fingerprint 04e6692e5c44347cdef3ff055c0cf966e6a50c079cad3d06d965f070f3683587. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 04e6692e5c44347cdef3ff055c0cf966e6a50c079cad3d06d965f070f3683587; artifact_sha256: 68bcaffb42002b53f8666b482f0c8eb740fd840065dd289e2b5fd57b6ee1fefd. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Brodland (2002) J. Biomech. Eng. Eqs. 1-4: Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) decomposing cell-cell interfacial tension into actomyosin cortical tension minus cadherin adhesion (gamma_{alpha,beta} = beta_alpha + beta_beta - omega_{alpha,beta}). | Krieg et al. (2008) Nature Cell Biology Figs. 1-4: AFM cortical tension hierarchy across zebrafish shield-stage germ-layer progenitors (beta_ectoderm ~ 50 < beta_mesoderm ~ 95 < beta_endoderm ~ 130 pN/um), concentric 3-germ-layer sorting, Blebbistatin Myosin-II inhibition arrest, and caMLCK ectodermal cortical stiffening sorting reversal. | Maître et al. (2012) Science Eq. 1: Young-Dupré cell-doublet contact angle cos(theta) = 1 - gamma_cc/(2*gamma_cm) and normalized contact radius r_c/R = sin(theta).; reconstructed_in_script: 2D deformable DITH cell sorting across all 4 perturbation regimes (wild-type engulfment, caMLCK cortex reversal, Blebbistatin Myosin-II inhibition, and high-HIT mushroom doublet) plus simultaneous 3-germ-layer concentric stratification (r_E = 0.870 > r_M = 0.663 > r_N = 0.446), a 7-point continuous beta_E sweep across the sorting inversion threshold beta_E = beta_M = 95 pN/um, and the Young-Dupré doublet contact curve. | Computer-vision segmentation of zebrafish blastoderm cross-transplantation GFP/RFP micrographs (`germ_layer_doublet_specimen.jpg`) across both layered engulfment (Row B, radial profile r = 0.9301, RMSE = 0.1844) and the protruding mushroom doublet (Row C, empirical r_c/R = 0.9717).; transfer_boundary: 2D lattice DITH representation of 3D zebrafish germ-layer progenitor reaggregates and blastoderm cross-transplants.; does_not_claim: Does not model sub-second single-molecule E-cadherin bond rupture kinetics or whole-embryo epiboly yolk-syncytial-layer microtubule pulling.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple DITH cortical tension dynamics to time-dependent Nodal/TGF-beta morphogen signaling gradients during zebrafish shield-stage internalization." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.13e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

